dsh-jingshen 0.4.3 · 精神

This is an independently adapted personal plugin, not an official DeepSeek product.
It incorporates code from deepseek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype under the MIT license.
Upstream snapshot: 8c32a9dc5d72c033816c6a8110b37f40cf94fba4
Upstream URL: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype
The upstream LICENSE is included unchanged.

The personal bundle reuses the upstream transactional Engine, SQLite Store and
Effects queue. Necessary upstream source and migration assets are included in
upstream/; PROVENANCE.json records small Harness API and asset-path adaptations.
Conversation delivery, delegation and session-local model selection use DeepSeek Harness 0.2.2-rc.5.
The GitHub/Feishu watchers, team setup, team prompts and upstream management UI are not mounted.

The interpretation of Hegel and the new experience, memory, runtime and UI code belong
to this adaptation. No claim is made that the software literally has consciousness,
reproduces the philosophical necessity of the Phenomenology, or attains absolute knowing.

Live vision uses the Apache-2.0 MediaPipe Tasks runtime and TensorFlow's
EfficientDet-Lite0 detector. The detector, its attribution and its license are
in src/vision-assets/. Character artwork was generated for this adaptation
using the visual reference provided by its author.

Default call synthesis uses the Breeze Blue cloud API with the public catalog
voice 大肥鱼（迷糊版）, voc_8yud7hz7c9q2. The service and hosted voice are
provided by Breeze Blue under its own terms. Official voice page:
https://breezeblue.ai/zh/voice-library/dafeiyu-dreamy-girl-voice-v8yud7hz7c9q2

The optional local voice assets include Luigi's single-speaker PrimeTTS v1b 16 kHz
Apache-2.0 model. Large weights are packed as float16 for storage and restored
to float32 for inference. The license, pronunciation data notices and upstream
training credits, including Inflect-Nano-v1, VoxCPM2 and Common Voice zh-TW,
are in media/voice/local/tts/NOTICE.txt and the accompanying license files.
The Mandarin frontend bundles pinyin-pro 3.29.5 under its MIT license. See
scripts/local-speech/pinyin/LICENSE and scripts/local-speech/pinyin/provenance.json.

Default speech recognition uses the Apache-2.0
sherpa-onnx-streaming-zipformer-small-ctc-zh-int8-2025-04-01 model and
vocabulary. See media/voice/local/asr/NOTICE and media/voice/local/asr/LICENSE
for the source, license and checksums. The recognizer uses the Sherpa-ONNX
native runtime available to DeepSeek Harness 0.2.2-rc.5.

ONNX Runtime Web is provided by Microsoft under the MIT license. The optional
CPU WebAssembly runtime and its loader are accompanied by scripts/local-speech/ort/LICENSE
and scripts/local-speech/ort/ThirdPartyNotices.txt.
Source: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

The optional 0.4.1 character reference was generated from original dialogue and
acting directions with Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign (Apache-2.0). Its sample and the
reference provenance are recorded in scripts/character-voice/voice.json.
The opt-in legacy voice setup downloads the k2-fsa Emilia-trained ZipVoice
Distill model (CC BY-NC) and the Vocos 24 kHz vocoder separately.
Model terms: https://huggingface.co/k2-fsa/ZipVoice#4-license
Vocoder: https://huggingface.co/charactr/vocos-mel-24khz
